questions.questionText:
Let $$A = \left( {\matrix{
2 & { - 2} \cr
1 & { - 1} \cr

} } \right)$$ and $$B = \left( {\matrix{
{ - 1} & 2 \cr
{ - 1} & 2 \cr

} } \right)$$. Then the number of elements in the set {(n, m) : n, m $$\in$$ {1, 2, .........., 10} and nAn + mBm = I} is ____________.

questions.explanationText:
$${A^2} = \left[ {\matrix{
2 & { - 2} \cr
1 & { - 1} \cr

} } \right]\left[ {\matrix{
2 & { - 2} \cr
1 & { - 1} \cr

} } \right] = \left[ {\matrix{
2 & { - 2} \cr
1 & { - 1} \cr

} } \right] = A$$

$$ \Rightarrow {A^K} = A,\,K \in I$$

$${B^2} = \left[ {\matrix{
{ - 1} & 2 \cr
{ - 1} & 2 \cr

} } \right]\left[ {\matrix{
{ - 1} & 2 \cr
{ - 1} & 2 \cr

} } \right] = \left[ {\matrix{
{ - 1} & 2 \cr
{ - 1} & 2 \cr

} } \right] = B$$

So, $${B^K} = B,\,K \in I$$

$$n{A^n} + m{B^m} = nA + mB$$

$$ = \left[ {\matrix{
{2n - 2n} \cr
{n - n} \cr

} } \right] + \left[ {\matrix{
{ - m} & {2m} \cr
{ - m} & {2m} \cr

} } \right]$$

$$ = \left[ {\matrix{
1 & 0 \cr
0 & 1 \cr

} } \right]$$

So, $$2n - m = 1,\, - n + m = 0,\,2m - n = 1$$

So, $$(m,n) = (1,1)$$

